# 2. Line Plot

```python
plt.plot(
    [1,2,3],
    [10,20,30],
    label="Trend",
    color="orange",
    linestyle="--",
    marker="o"
)

plt.title("Line Plot")

plt.xlabel("X-axis")

plt.ylabel("Y-axis")

plt.legend()

plt.show()
```

---

## Components

### plot()

```python
plt.plot(x,y)
```

Creates a line graph.

---

### label

```python
label="Trend"
```

Used in legend.

Output:

```text
Trend
```

appears in graph legend.

---

### color

```python
color="orange"
```

Changes line color.

Examples:

```python
color="red"
color="blue"
color="green"
color="black"
```

---

### linestyle

```python
linestyle="--"
```

Line style.

Examples:

```python
"-"   Solid Line

"--"  Dashed Line

":"   Dotted Line

"-."  Dash Dot
```

---

### marker

```python
marker="o"
```

Marks each data point.

Examples:

```python
"o" Circle

"s" Square

"*" Star

"+" Plus
```

---

### title

```python
plt.title("Line Plot")
```

Graph heading.

---

### xlabel

```python
plt.xlabel("X-axis")
```

Name of X-axis.

---

### ylabel

```python
plt.ylabel("Y-axis")
```

Name of Y-axis.

---

### legend

```python
plt.legend()
```

Shows labels.

---

### Memory

```text
plot()
↓
Line Graph

title()
↓
Heading

xlabel()
↓
X-axis Name

ylabel()
↓
Y-axis Name

legend()
↓
Show Labels
```

