# 3. Bar Chart

```python
categories = ["A","B","C"]

values = [10,15,17]

plt.bar(
    categories,
    values,
    color="blue"
)

plt.title("Bar Chart")

plt.show()
```

### Meaning

```text
A = 10

B = 15

C = 17
```

Creates bars.

### Memory

```text
bar()
↓
Compare Categories
```

### Use Cases

```text
Department Sales

Student Marks

Product Revenue
```

---

# 4. Histogram

```python
data = [1,2,2,3,3,3,4,4,4,4]

plt.hist(
    data,
    bins=4,
    color="green",
    edgecolor="black"
)

plt.title("Histogram")

plt.show()
```

---

## bins

```python
bins=4
```

Creates 4 intervals.

Example:

```text
1-2

2-3

3-4

4-5
```

---

## edgecolor

```python
edgecolor="black"
```

Bar border color.

---

### Purpose

Show data distribution.

### Memory

```text
hist()
↓
Distribution
```

Questions answered:

```text
Most Common Value?

Data Spread?

Frequency?
```

