# 5. Scatter Plot

⚠️ Small mistake in your code.

You created:

```python
x1 = [1,2,3,4,5]

y1 = [10,12,25,30,45]
```

But used:

```python
plt.scatter(x,y)
```

Should be:

```python
plt.scatter(x1,y1)
```

---

### Correct Code

```python
x1 = [1,2,3,4,5]

y1 = [10,12,25,30,45]

plt.scatter(
    x1,
    y1,
    color="red"
)

plt.title("Scatter Plot")

plt.xlabel("X-axis Label")

plt.ylabel("Y-axis Label")

plt.legend(["Dataset 1"])

plt.show()
```

---

### Meaning

Plots individual points.

```text
(1,10)

(2,12)

(3,25)

(4,30)

(5,45)
```

---

### Use Cases

```text
Age vs Salary

Height vs Weight

Study Hours vs Marks
```

---

### Memory

```text
scatter()
↓
Relationship Between Variables
```

